TN-Eval  (rubric, SOAP prompt, scoring prompts)
  Apache License 2.0 -- https://github.com/amazon-science/TN-Eval

  Note: the licence covers the CODE repository, which is where the prompts and
  the rubric come from. The notes and human annotations live in a separate
  repository, TN-Eval-Data, which publishes no licence -- verified 2026-08-24.
  They are fetched at run time and never redistributed here.
  Shah, Raj Sanjay; Xu, Lei; Liu, Qianchu; Burnsky, Jon; Bertagnolli, Drew;
  Shivade, Chaitanya. "TN-Eval: Rubric and Evaluation Protocols for Measuring
  the Quality of Behavioral Therapy Notes." ACL 2025, Industry Track.

  This repository reproduces TN-Eval's rubric text, SOAP generation prompt and
  scoring prompts. They are used under the Apache-2.0 licence, unmodified in
  wording, with the model backend replaced (AWS Bedrock -> OpenAI-compatible).

